.TH MYFPAC.SH 1 "15 October 2026" Linux "FPAC Operator's Manual"
.SH NAME
myfpac.sh \- Bash shell script to control FPAC application daemons.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B myfpac.sh start|stop|restart|status
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
.B myfpac.sh
Starts/stops the application daemons of an FPAC node. The AX.25 link layer
(kissattach, ax25ipd, netromd, ...) is managed separately by ax25up/ax25stop
and is deliberately left running.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP 10
.BI "\ Start -"
Start FPAC - Start up elements of the FPAC node
.TP 
.BI "\ Stop -"
Stop - FPAC - Shutdown Node
.TP 11
.BI "\ Restart -"
Restart - Stop then Start FPAC.
.TP 10
.BI "\ Status -"
Display the Status of FPAC elements.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/etc/ax25/myfpac.conf
Settings of the node, read at each run and never overwritten by an update
(make install writes myfpac.sh again). Shell variables, for instance:
.EX
SYSOP="F6BVP"
CONNECT="rose0 F6BVP-1 2080175520"
.EE
When CONNECT is set, each start leaves the message "FPAC node <host>
started" to SYSOP on that BBS with mailbbs(1); CONNECT holds the port, the
callsign of the BBS and, for ROSE, its address.
.TP
.I /var/log/fpac.log
What myfpac.sh did, and the answer of mailbbs.
.SH AUTHOR
Bernard Pidoux F6BVP <bernard.f6bvp@gmail.com>
